{
  "decision_conditions": [
    "Reason : 1 - The proposed development, by reason of its scale, massing and siting, would form a visually over dominant and discordant addition that would fail to appear as a subservient addition within the original site. The outbuilding would result in harm to the character and appearance of the spatial setting and street scene. The proposal is therefore contrary to policies LP1 and LP5 of the Wandsworth Local Plan (2023) and the Housing SPD (2016).",
    "Reason : 2 - The proposed development, by reason of its scale, massing and siting would be an unneighbourly form of development that creates a pronounced sense of enclosure and appears overbearing to occupiers of neighbouring properties, resulting in harm to their residential amenity. The proposal is therefore contrary to policy LP2 of the Wandsworth Local Plan (2023). ",
    "Reason : 3 - In dealing with this application the Council has implemented the requirement in the National Planning Policy Framework to make available detailed advice in the form of our statutory policies in the Local Plan as well as offering a full pre application advice service. However, we have been unable to seek solutions to problems as the principle of the proposal is clearly contrary to our statutory policies and negotiation could not overcome the reasons for refusal."
  ],
